{
  "id": 22,
  "name": "cluster_aware_progress_regret",
  "intent": "Add a constant cluster_density bonus to the parent's progress-scaled return/regret structure. Candidates surrounded by more unvisited peers within mean distance score higher, biasing construction toward dense intra-cluster regions where completing neighborhood travel before inter-cluster jumps is optimal for the target family. The constant offset is nearly invariant on grid instances (cluster_density ~ uniform across candidates), preserving the parent's grid strength. On clustered and uniform instances, it introduces a useful ranking gradient that complements return/regret dynamics without diluting the progress modulation.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "regret"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    dist = f['distance']\n    ret = f['return_distance']\n    prog = f['progress']\n    regret = f['regret']\n    density = f['cluster_density']\n    return_coeff = 0.20 + 0.25 * prog\n    regret_coeff = 0.05 + 0.25 * prog\n    return -dist + return_coeff * ret + regret_coeff * regret + 0.15 * density",
  "source": "live_llm",
